markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Interactivity in Web Apps</h1>

<p>When you visit a website or open an app, you're not just looking at information, you're doing something with it. Interactivity is what turns a static page into an engaging experience. It's what allows users to click, tap, type, scroll, or hover to make something happen.</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px;">
<p>📖 <b>Interactivity</b> is the ability of a software application or website to respond to user input.</p>
</div>

<details style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 20px 0;">
<summary style="cursor: pointer; font-weight: bold; color: #1F1976;">⚡ Interactive Elements in Web Apps</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 12px;">
<p>Interactive elements come in many forms:</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Buttons</b> that trigger actions</li>
<li><b>Menus</b> that expand or collapse</li>
<li><b>Search bars</b> that respond as you type</li>
<li><b>Icons</b> that change color or shape when hovered over</li>
</ul>
<p>These small moments of feedback and response are what make a web app feel alive and user-friendly.</p>
</div>
</details>

<p>Below, try spotting interactivity yourself. Hover or click around the mock site and see what you find.</p>

